  "notes": "A panel / side panels screen from Framework7's kitchen sink, shown with Framework7's iOS or Material (Android) theme. Framework7 builds mobile apps (and PWAs / Capacitor apps) from HTML.\n\nUse: npm i framework7, then the same markup inside a Framework7 app. Docs: https://framework7.io/docs/",
  "code": "<div class=\"page\" id=\"panel-page\">\n  <div class=\"navbar\">\n    <div class=\"navbar-bg\"></div>\n    <div class=\"navbar-inner sliding\">\n      <div class=\"left\">\n        <a class=\"link back\">\n          <i class=\"icon icon-back\"></i>\n\n        </a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"title\">Panel / Side panels</div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"panel panel-left panel-cover panel-init\" id=\"panel-nested\" data-container-el=\"#panel-page\">\n    <div class=\"page\">\n      <div class=\"page-content\">\n        <div class=\"block block-strong-ios block-outline-ios\">\n          <p>This is page-nested Panel.</p>\n          <p><a class=\"panel-close\">Close me</a></p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"page-content\">\n    <div class=\"block block-strong inset\">\n      <p>Framework7 comes with 2 panels (on left and on right), both are optional.\n        You can put absolutely anything inside: data lists, forms, custom content, and even other isolated app view\n        (like in right panel now) with its own dynamic navbar.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"block block-strong inset\">\n      <p class=\"grid grid-cols-2 grid-gap\">\n        <a class=\"button button-round button-fill panel-open\">Open left panel</a>\n        <a class=\"button button-round button-fill panel-open\" data-panel=\"right\">Open right panel</a>\n      </p>\n      <p>\n        <a class=\"button button-round button-fill panel-open\" data-panel=\"#panel-nested\">Open nested panel</a>\n      </p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>",
